WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.660
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.680 --> 00:03.330
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:03.350 --> 00:05.000
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:05.060 --> 00:06.580
What did you feel

6
00:06.600 --> 00:08.660
when you were close to her?

7
00:08.680 --> 00:09.800
I wanted to stop,

8
00:10.160 --> 00:11.400
but I couldn't.

9
00:11.600 --> 00:13.140
I couldn't stop myself.

10
00:13.160 --> 00:15.860
I know your body is rejecting this...

11
00:15.880 --> 00:18.840
I'll make you want to hug me.

12
00:18.860 --> 00:20.760
I was in a car accident several years ago.

13
00:21.000 --> 00:22.340
My doctor said the accident made me

14
00:22.360 --> 00:24.200
reject physical contact.

15
00:27.600 --> 00:29.060
What did you feel

16
00:29.080 --> 00:31.240
when you were close to her?

17
00:31.680 --> 00:32.840
I wanted to stop,

18
00:33.560 --> 00:34.840
but I couldn't.

19
00:36.000 --> 00:37.480
I couldn't stop myself.

20
00:38.160 --> 00:39.600
This is your life.

21
00:39.920 --> 00:42.800
Are you going to let guilt stop you from being happy?

22
00:43.480 --> 00:45.840
If someone who saved me isn't happy,

23
00:46.120 --> 00:47.720
then how could I be happy?

24
00:50.400 --> 00:51.480
I'm sorry.

25
00:52.920 --> 00:54.160
I can't do this.

26
01:04.820 --> 01:06.080
I have a girlfriend.

27
01:18.680 --> 01:20.680
[Third Person]

28
01:22.980 --> 01:32.800
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

29
01:32.820 --> 01:37.920
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

30
01:37.940 --> 01:41.820
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

31
01:42.100 --> 01:48.100
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

32
01:48.120 --> 01:57.820
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

33
01:57.840 --> 02:02.880
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

34
02:02.900 --> 02:07.180
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

35
02:07.200 --> 02:15.840
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

36
02:16.360 --> 02:25.000
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

37
02:40.120 --> 02:41.760
I had been dating my girlfriend for a long time

38
02:42.600 --> 02:45.240
until an accident happened four years ago.

39
02:48.400 --> 02:50.520
I lost my memories.

40
02:52.280 --> 02:53.680
I forgot everything,

41
02:57.740 --> 02:59.440
including my girlfriend.

42
03:00.700 --> 03:02.700
She always took care of me,

43
03:04.500 --> 03:06.500
but my memories never returned.

44
03:07.920 --> 03:10.320
I can't remember the love I had for her,

45
03:13.600 --> 03:15.560
and we always argued.

46
03:17.900 --> 03:19.900
I actually asked to break up,

47
03:22.780 --> 03:25.320
but her parents pressured me.

48
03:26.040 --> 03:27.680
So I had to stay with her.

49
03:30.200 --> 03:31.720
It sounds like an excuse,

50
03:35.760 --> 03:37.400
but it's the truth.

51
03:38.640 --> 03:40.400
Things are complicated.

52
03:42.240 --> 03:44.520
It feels like it's over, but it isn't.

53
03:45.580 --> 03:47.820
And I don't know when it will actually end.

54
03:51.100 --> 03:52.780
So you want to stop what happens between us?

55
03:57.520 --> 03:58.980
I'm so sorry.

56
04:01.520 --> 04:03.680
I don't want to wrong you and her any further.

57
04:09.200 --> 04:12.220
I don't want you to be in this terrible relationship.

58
04:14.980 --> 04:17.520
Someone sweet like you deserves good love.

59
04:18.800 --> 04:20.400
That doesn't come from you.

60
04:24.960 --> 04:26.080
I'm sorry...

61
04:27.680 --> 04:31.240
I'm not in a state to give anyone good love.

62
04:37.040 --> 04:38.360
So what should we do now?

63
04:41.180 --> 04:42.600
Should we end it here

64
04:44.000 --> 04:45.520
and never meet again?

65
04:51.040 --> 04:52.360
It's up to you.

66
05:02.140 --> 05:03.760
Then, do you still want to be friends?

67
05:07.280 --> 05:08.480
Of course I do.

68
05:12.680 --> 05:14.040
But do you...

69
05:15.440 --> 05:17.440
want to be friends with someone like me?

70
05:19.480 --> 05:20.720
What does

71
05:21.440 --> 05:22.760
"someone like you" mean?

72
05:25.560 --> 05:27.240
A worthless person

73
05:28.160 --> 05:29.560
who is unemployed

74
05:30.560 --> 05:32.360
and never felt like they fit in anywhere.

75
05:35.380 --> 05:37.720
It's like wearing a bra that's the wrong size all the time?

76
05:40.420 --> 05:42.720
Sometimes it feels empty,

77
05:44.400 --> 05:46.660
but sometimes it's uncomfortable.

78
05:58.560 --> 05:59.440
Where are you going?

79
06:08.040 --> 06:09.240
Sun, what are you doing?

80
06:12.360 --> 06:14.560
If you can't pick the right bra, then let me help you.

81
06:19.360 --> 06:21.360
You have to find the right size.

82
06:23.660 --> 06:26.000
Explore what you can do.

83
06:27.520 --> 06:28.680
I don't think

84
06:29.120 --> 06:30.380
you're worthless.

85
06:32.700 --> 06:34.640
You were just in the wrong place.

86
06:40.760 --> 06:43.200
You have to choose a bra that suits your breast shape.

87
06:44.000 --> 06:46.400
If you know what your strong suit is,

88
06:47.240 --> 06:49.360
you'll know where you should be.

89
06:54.160 --> 06:56.760
Lastly... try it out first.

90
06:58.240 --> 06:59.920
If you feel uncomfortable,

91
07:04.900 --> 07:06.600
it's okay to run away.

92
07:08.060 --> 07:10.000
If the bra really is bad,

93
07:10.860 --> 07:12.080
maybe...

94
07:13.140 --> 07:15.140
it's better to discard it.

95
07:17.280 --> 07:18.000
Mm.

96
07:18.280 --> 07:19.280
I understand now.

97
07:20.840 --> 07:21.920
I don't know

98
07:22.060 --> 07:24.200
when I'll find a bra that fits.

99
07:29.920 --> 07:31.640
But your necklace

100
07:32.680 --> 07:34.880
never felt uncomfortable.

101
07:36.040 --> 07:37.800
I really want to be your friend.

102
07:40.600 --> 07:42.840
Because you pity someone who can't choose her own bra?

103
07:43.960 --> 07:44.800
No.

104
07:45.960 --> 07:47.960
It's because you were willing to listen

105
07:48.280 --> 07:49.640
to what I was saying.

106
07:51.640 --> 07:54.140
Even though you didn't have to do that.

107
07:56.120 --> 07:58.760
You make the person you're with feel seen

108
07:59.400 --> 08:00.720
and acknowledged.

109
08:01.760 --> 08:02.560
That's the reason

110
08:02.860 --> 08:04.760
I want to be your friend.

111
08:15.260 --> 08:17.000
Will you run tomorrow?

112
08:17.280 --> 08:18.360
I don't know.

113
08:18.500 --> 08:19.680
I don't want to promise anything.

114
08:21.680 --> 08:23.280
How about... the day after tomorrow?

115
08:25.960 --> 08:27.140
I don't know.

116
08:27.160 --> 08:28.240
It depends if I have work or not.

117
08:31.520 --> 08:32.520
Okay.

118
08:44.700 --> 08:46.700
I'll get going now.

119
08:47.240 --> 08:48.680
Um, Chris?

120
08:48.900 --> 08:50.400
Can I have your phone?

121
08:56.080 --> 08:57.040
Here.

122
09:12.640 --> 09:14.720
If you want to know if I'm running tomorrow,

123
09:14.740 --> 09:15.840
you can call me.

124
09:17.760 --> 09:18.760
Okay.

125
09:19.880 --> 09:21.020
Your "okay" this time

126
09:21.040 --> 09:22.600
sounds much more cheerful than earlier.

127
09:24.080 --> 09:26.520
Next time, if you want something, just tell me.

128
09:26.920 --> 09:28.320
We're friends now.

129
09:28.900 --> 09:30.240
We can talk about anything.

130
09:31.060 --> 09:32.800
Do you understand, friend?

131
09:36.280 --> 09:38.040
Yes, friend.

132
09:46.720 --> 09:50.640
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

133
09:59.620 --> 10:00.320
Nadear,

134
10:01.480 --> 10:03.600
why did we co-own this restaurant?

135
10:04.740 --> 10:06.400
You've asked me before, haven't you?

136
10:07.920 --> 10:09.140
Are you annoyed

137
10:09.160 --> 10:11.320
that you've had to answer the same question for years?

138
10:13.660 --> 10:15.960
I'm glad you care, actually.

139
10:17.360 --> 10:19.120
It makes me feel hopeful.

140
10:21.620 --> 10:23.620
We opened this restaurant together

141
10:24.880 --> 10:25.800
because

142
10:25.960 --> 10:29.640
you've wanted to have your own business since you were a student.

143
10:30.200 --> 10:31.960
After we graduated,

144
10:32.120 --> 10:33.740
Nan asked if we wanted to open a restaurant,

145
10:33.760 --> 10:35.520
so the three of us decided to invest together.

146
10:39.800 --> 10:41.360
Were the three of us rich?

147
10:42.980 --> 10:45.200
We borrowed money from our parents to invest.

148
10:45.880 --> 10:47.160
It was very risky,

149
10:47.880 --> 10:49.300
but it worked out.

150
10:50.680 --> 10:52.800
We already paid our parents back in full.

151
10:56.000 --> 10:57.880
Before you got hurt,

152
10:58.720 --> 11:00.840
our restaurant was very profitable.

153
11:04.160 --> 11:06.040
Does that mean it's not as profitable now?

154
11:07.280 --> 11:08.160
Why?

155
11:08.800 --> 11:10.320
Is there a problem?

156
11:14.140 --> 11:16.240
Just the usual problems, Chris.

157
11:16.660 --> 11:18.480
The economy is bad,

158
11:19.240 --> 11:21.280
so people don't eat out as much.

159
11:23.000 --> 11:25.120
But I've seen that we have a lot of customers every day.

160
11:25.760 --> 11:28.040
You weren't here when we had no customers.

161
11:31.560 --> 11:32.320
Alright,

162
11:32.680 --> 11:35.000
then I'll come to our restaurant every day.

163
11:36.400 --> 11:37.440
You don't have to do that.

164
11:38.520 --> 11:40.320
You're still recovering,

165
11:40.880 --> 11:42.520
so I don't want you to be stressed.

166
11:43.400 --> 11:44.340
But I want to help...

167
11:44.360 --> 11:46.000
I got this,

168
11:47.760 --> 11:49.660
but I want to focus on work for now.

169
11:49.680 --> 11:51.320
Let's talk later, alright, Chris?

170
12:11.160 --> 12:12.020
Nan,

171
12:12.120 --> 12:13.960
- Hm? - can I talk to you about our restaurant?

172
12:14.800 --> 12:15.680
What do you want to know?

173
12:17.000 --> 12:18.200
I can't remember anything,

174
12:18.220 --> 12:19.720
so can you start from the beginning?

175
12:19.860 --> 12:21.260
Whoa, that was years ago.

176
12:21.280 --> 12:22.480
Why do you want to know now?

177
12:22.960 --> 12:24.320
Of course I want to know.

178
12:24.720 --> 12:25.760
Just tell me.

179
12:27.760 --> 12:30.600
It started when we went to a party together.

180
12:30.620 --> 12:33.200
I... was Nadear's senior buddy.

181
12:34.100 --> 12:35.600
Mm, I know that.

182
12:36.600 --> 12:38.500
I told her...

183
12:38.520 --> 12:40.000
I want to open my own restaurant.

184
12:40.100 --> 12:42.280
You and Nadear were interested, so we started it together.

185
12:42.800 --> 12:44.800
It was going to fail at first, because...

186
12:44.920 --> 12:47.280
we couldn't find a good spot at a reasonable price.

187
12:47.740 --> 12:49.740
Until you told me to rent this place.

188
12:51.440 --> 12:52.740
I didn't know that.

189
12:52.760 --> 12:54.280
Nadear never told me about this.

190
12:55.940 --> 12:57.360
You told me

191
12:57.560 --> 12:59.560
your friend recommended this spot.

192
13:00.920 --> 13:02.000
Which friend?

193
13:02.520 --> 13:05.760
I don't know. Ask your girlfriend. Maybe she knows.

194
13:07.120 --> 13:09.080
Can I talk to her in private?

195
13:11.260 --> 13:12.120
Of course.

196
13:21.240 --> 13:23.640
Can you stop asking others about our restaurant?

197
13:24.280 --> 13:25.680
It doesn't sit well with me.

198
13:26.440 --> 13:29.000
It looks like you don't know anything about our restaurant.

199
13:30.260 --> 13:33.280
Well, I don't know anything because you never have time to tell me anything.

200
13:34.860 --> 13:36.220
If I'm free,

201
13:36.240 --> 13:38.040
I'll gladly tell you about it.

202
13:38.270 --> 13:40.880
Why wouldn't I want you to know more about our restaurant?

203
13:41.920 --> 13:43.520
I'm busy,

204
13:43.950 --> 13:46.080
and you're not well.

205
13:46.920 --> 13:49.280
I want you to gradually remember everything,

206
13:51.040 --> 13:53.060
or maybe wait for me to tell you,

207
13:53.080 --> 13:54.880
instead of learning things by asking other people.

208
13:55.920 --> 13:57.480
Then does that mean if I can't remember,

209
13:57.680 --> 13:59.840
I don't have the right to know anything about our restaurant?

210
14:01.860 --> 14:03.680
I don't want to be like this forever.

211
14:03.700 --> 14:04.960
I want to be normal.

212
14:05.600 --> 14:07.280
I want to know what I did in the past.

213
14:07.300 --> 14:08.800
I want to know everything.

214
14:08.980 --> 14:12.160
I don't want to keep trying to remember things, but nothing comes to mind.

215
14:13.200 --> 14:14.720
Don't you get it?

216
14:19.800 --> 14:20.960
Okay, Chris,

217
14:23.520 --> 14:24.840
from now on,

218
14:25.180 --> 14:27.280
I'll answer all of your questions.

219
14:30.900 --> 14:33.200
Then... which one of my friends told us to rent this place?

220
14:38.420 --> 14:40.960
Chris suddenly became interested in our restaurant.

221
14:41.280 --> 14:43.120
She asked me so many questions.

222
14:43.980 --> 14:46.680
Doesn't that mean Chris is interested in you?

223
14:49.200 --> 14:50.400
No.

224
14:52.060 --> 14:55.000
It means Chris is trying to be independent.

225
14:57.320 --> 14:59.120
She doesn't want to depend on me.

226
15:02.680 --> 15:04.240
What did you make of that?

227
15:05.300 --> 15:07.300
She's practically trying to break up with me.

228
15:13.500 --> 15:14.640
You're overthinking it.

229
15:15.060 --> 15:16.840
Chris is perfectly fine.

230
15:17.240 --> 15:19.680
She thought I cared about her again,

231
15:20.480 --> 15:23.000
but I really don't feel anything towards her anymore.

232
15:23.960 --> 15:25.880
I'm just trying to live my life.

233
15:28.460 --> 15:30.640
Is this what you call giving her false hope?

234
15:32.300 --> 15:35.000
How can you stop someone from hoping?

235
15:36.720 --> 15:38.880
Follow your heart.

236
15:40.080 --> 15:41.480
If you don't feel anything,

237
15:42.000 --> 15:44.120
then show her that you don't.

238
15:45.500 --> 15:47.600
Nadear will definitely understand.

239
15:51.920 --> 15:53.520
I don't want to upset her.

240
15:55.360 --> 15:56.680
Then are you upset

241
15:57.120 --> 15:59.080
that you didn't get to live the way you wanted?

242
16:00.440 --> 16:02.120
If you still hold each other back,

243
16:03.860 --> 16:05.520
no one is going to be happy.

244
16:08.420 --> 16:09.420
Right?

245
16:21.200 --> 16:22.860
As a doctor,

246
16:23.230 --> 16:25.280
what do you think?

247
16:27.080 --> 16:28.320
It's a good sign.

248
16:29.360 --> 16:31.560
She's trying to get into your world.

249
16:35.720 --> 16:36.720
Really?

250
16:38.600 --> 16:39.480
Yes.

251
16:40.500 --> 16:42.440
If there's something off,

252
16:43.640 --> 16:45.160
you'll be the first to know.

253
17:19.640 --> 17:22.120
Can you stop asking others about our restaurant?

254
17:22.440 --> 17:24.680
Then... which one of my friends told us to rent this place?

255
17:25.120 --> 17:26.480
I forgot.

256
17:27.120 --> 17:28.960
If I can remember, I'll tell you.

257
17:30.640 --> 17:33.400
Let's discuss what you want to know later.

258
17:36.000 --> 17:38.640
You make the person you're with feel seen

259
17:39.240 --> 17:40.720
and acknowledged.

260
17:41.660 --> 17:42.440
That's the reason

261
17:42.680 --> 17:44.680
I want to be your friend.

262
17:48.360 --> 17:50.080
Chris, you have to understand.

263
17:50.940 --> 17:52.800
I have important things to deal with right now.

264
18:08.520 --> 18:10.240
I just saw your call.

265
18:10.800 --> 18:12.060
If you're asking me to go running,

266
18:12.080 --> 18:13.320
I'll have to decline.

267
18:14.360 --> 18:15.360
Sun...

268
18:16.240 --> 18:17.900
can I come to your room?

269
18:31.280 --> 18:34.000
Tell me why you wanted to talk to me this early.

270
18:39.720 --> 18:41.640
I... want to talk to you.

271
18:43.180 --> 18:43.920
Alright,

272
18:44.360 --> 18:45.600
but let's not stand while we talk.

273
18:54.160 --> 18:55.620
When it's early like this...

274
18:55.640 --> 18:57.640
I don't want to deal with gravity yet.

275
18:58.500 --> 19:00.720
You can get straight to the point.

276
19:06.840 --> 19:09.080
I want to ask you something.

277
19:22.780 --> 19:25.200
Make some eye contact when you talk, friend.

278
19:30.480 --> 19:31.240
So,

279
19:31.480 --> 19:32.680
what would you like to talk about?

280
19:35.600 --> 19:38.230
[Third Person]

281
19:40.673 --> 19:43.273
[Third Person]

282
19:43.433 --> 19:45.713
So, what would you like to talk about?

283
19:47.313 --> 19:48.633
Why don't you say anything?

284
19:50.353 --> 19:51.873
Or...

285
19:52.513 --> 19:53.953
you want to do something else first?

286
19:59.993 --> 20:01.913
I want to do something else first.

287
20:08.313 --> 20:09.353
Ooh!

288
20:10.973 --> 20:12.593
Gay panic, huh?

289
20:14.633 --> 20:15.793
Tease me however you want.

290
20:16.233 --> 20:17.693
Alright, I'm ready.

291
20:25.593 --> 20:27.993
Sun... don't do this.

292
20:28.273 --> 20:30.153
I'm trying to hold myself back.

293
20:35.633 --> 20:37.753
Then when will you stop holding back?

294
20:38.513 --> 20:39.613
Sun...

295
20:45.973 --> 20:47.313
I'll stop.

296
20:49.493 --> 20:51.253
So, what do you want to talk about?

297
20:51.273 --> 20:52.193
Go ahead.

298
20:59.733 --> 21:00.673
Well...

299
21:01.113 --> 21:02.433
What would you do

300
21:03.143 --> 21:04.193
if you had a friend

301
21:04.213 --> 21:06.833
who wouldn't discuss anything important in your life

302
21:08.873 --> 21:11.453
because she always had other important things to do?

303
21:13.713 --> 21:14.633
Your girlfriend?

304
21:18.993 --> 21:21.153
If she won't discuss it with you,

305
21:21.473 --> 21:23.073
you'll have to make her realize

306
21:23.093 --> 21:24.233
you're important.

307
21:29.753 --> 21:31.753
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

308
21:38.873 --> 21:40.713
If she won't discuss it with you,

309
21:40.973 --> 21:42.593
you'll have to get her attention.

310
21:43.393 --> 21:44.433
How?

311
21:44.673 --> 21:45.833
I'll show you.

312
21:46.113 --> 21:48.073
You'll play someone who's strong-willed.

313
21:48.873 --> 21:49.753
Easy.

314
21:49.993 --> 21:51.413
I'm very strong-willed.

315
21:51.433 --> 21:53.113
You won't sway me.

316
22:05.753 --> 22:07.753
See? I don't feel anything.

317
22:08.293 --> 22:09.233
Hey,

318
22:09.853 --> 22:11.233
that's no fun.

319
22:18.993 --> 22:19.793
Sun!

320
22:21.013 --> 22:21.873
Sun.

321
22:23.553 --> 22:24.673
Are you alright?

322
22:26.013 --> 22:26.913
Success!

323
22:28.173 --> 22:30.193
Oh, so you tricked me?

324
22:31.193 --> 22:33.073
Would I even get your attention otherwise?

325
22:34.193 --> 22:36.833
Why don't you do what your friend wants you to do?

326
22:37.873 --> 22:39.353
Maybe she'll drop everything

327
22:39.373 --> 22:40.793
and take an interest in you.

328
22:54.033 --> 22:54.973
Leave it to me.

329
23:01.293 --> 23:02.313
What happened?

330
23:02.773 --> 23:04.373
I wanted to ask you that too.

331
23:04.393 --> 23:06.873
Chris suddenly swooped in to serve that dish.

332
23:17.013 --> 23:17.793
Chris,

333
23:18.793 --> 23:19.873
what are you doing?

334
23:21.073 --> 23:22.473
I'm serving food.

335
23:22.833 --> 23:23.993
I'm serious.

336
23:25.113 --> 23:26.553
Isn't this our restaurant?

337
23:26.573 --> 23:27.993
I have to work, don't I?

338
23:32.673 --> 23:33.673
One moment, please.

339
23:37.473 --> 23:38.473
What would you like?

340
23:40.833 --> 23:42.433
What's gotten into her?

341
23:42.633 --> 23:43.633
She's enthusiastic.

342
23:44.833 --> 23:46.153
Has she recovered?

343
23:46.253 --> 23:47.833
That's why you let her work, right?

344
24:04.773 --> 24:06.773
One Wagyu green curry and soda set.

345
24:10.313 --> 24:11.873
Can we talk?

346
24:16.973 --> 24:18.973
Do I have to do something you don't like

347
24:19.233 --> 24:20.793
before you'll have time to talk to me?

348
24:22.233 --> 24:23.553
Are you going to stop me again?

349
24:24.513 --> 24:25.753
I'm not,

350
24:26.633 --> 24:28.873
but we already have a lot of waiters.

351
24:29.233 --> 24:30.513
If you want to work,

352
24:30.533 --> 24:32.433
go back to what you were doing.

353
24:34.053 --> 24:35.313
What I was doing?

354
24:36.293 --> 24:37.893
Behind-the-scenes stuff, marketing.

355
24:37.913 --> 24:40.073
Thinking of new ways to attract customers.

356
24:41.193 --> 24:43.033
If you can do it,

357
24:43.773 --> 24:45.673
you can come back to work as before.

358
24:54.473 --> 24:55.113
Let's go.

359
24:56.013 --> 24:57.753
- The movie was fun, yeah? - Mm.

360
24:59.933 --> 25:01.253
I'll see you tomorrow.

361
25:01.273 --> 25:01.873
Okay.

362
25:02.013 --> 25:03.113
Drive home safe.

363
25:12.913 --> 25:13.713
Chris!

364
25:19.673 --> 25:20.913
When did you get here?

365
25:22.953 --> 25:25.393
I arrived just as you came down with that woman.

366
25:26.313 --> 25:27.713
Why didn't you greet me then?

367
25:28.273 --> 25:29.193
That's Oil,

368
25:29.333 --> 25:30.313
my best friend.

369
25:31.193 --> 25:31.953
"Friend"?

370
25:32.873 --> 25:34.233
Mm, friend.

371
25:34.433 --> 25:35.633
Just like you.

372
25:43.373 --> 25:45.373
Did you come to see me about something?

373
25:48.593 --> 25:51.073
Congratulations, you got back to work.

374
25:52.173 --> 25:53.313
It's because of you.

375
25:53.793 --> 25:56.593
Without you, I'd probably be living without a goal.

376
25:57.553 --> 25:59.473
You gave me a goal in life, too.

377
26:14.533 --> 26:15.353
One second.

378
26:23.553 --> 26:24.673
I bought you a sandwich.

379
26:24.833 --> 26:25.873
Thanks.

380
26:26.613 --> 26:28.093
In case you're hungry tonight.

381
26:29.833 --> 26:30.833
There's something in your hair.

382
26:34.313 --> 26:35.993
Go rest up. Good night.

383
26:36.513 --> 26:37.253
Bye.

384
26:37.273 --> 26:38.433
- See you. - See you.

385
26:50.993 --> 26:51.793
Look.

386
26:52.873 --> 26:54.393
Isn't she extra?

387
26:54.633 --> 26:57.193
She still came back to get me this sandwich after she left.

388
26:58.353 --> 27:01.273
She's probably worried I might not have anything to eat

389
27:01.673 --> 27:03.553
because we have a date tomorrow morning.

390
27:06.233 --> 27:07.033
Date?

391
27:07.353 --> 27:08.033
Mm.

392
27:08.693 --> 27:09.913
A date to relieve some stress.

393
27:10.633 --> 27:11.993
Would you like to join us?

394
27:13.873 --> 27:14.913
Oil won't mind.

395
27:17.353 --> 27:19.513
It's okay, you guys go ahead.

396
27:34.793 --> 27:35.913
I changed my mind.

397
27:36.193 --> 27:37.433
May I join you?

398
27:45.073 --> 27:47.933
[Third Person]

399
27:50.382 --> 27:52.982
[Third Person]

400
27:55.542 --> 27:56.582
- Here are my papers. - Thank you.

401
27:56.602 --> 27:57.902
- I'll be in your care. - One moment, please.

402
27:58.862 --> 27:59.862
Oh, Sun.

403
28:03.602 --> 28:04.702
This is Oil.

404
28:04.802 --> 28:05.702
She's a doctor.

405
28:06.082 --> 28:07.122
We studied together,

406
28:07.382 --> 28:08.982
and she's also a shareholder in my clinic.

407
28:11.182 --> 28:12.662
Work is tough right now,

408
28:12.682 --> 28:15.142
so Oil invited me to take a flower arrangement class.

409
28:15.302 --> 28:17.022
She told me it helps relieve stress.

410
28:19.222 --> 28:20.482
I'm Chris.

411
28:20.902 --> 28:22.382
Can I join you today?

412
28:23.062 --> 28:24.182
You don't need my permission.

413
28:24.742 --> 28:26.142
Anyone can take the class.

414
28:27.342 --> 28:28.702
Just sign up there.

415
28:33.702 --> 28:34.662
Shall we...

416
28:35.382 --> 28:36.782
go look at the flowers inside?

417
28:44.862 --> 28:45.582
Mm.

418
28:47.662 --> 28:49.342
Go ahead, I'll sign up first.

419
28:52.702 --> 28:54.302
Chris can take care of herself,

420
28:54.662 --> 28:55.422
right?

421
28:59.402 --> 29:00.302
Let's go.

422
29:10.142 --> 29:11.502
Alright, everyone,

423
29:11.522 --> 29:14.362
before we start arranging the flowers,

424
29:14.382 --> 29:15.902
I want you to picture

425
29:15.922 --> 29:17.522
who you want to give these flowers to

426
29:17.542 --> 29:18.822
and why.

427
29:19.022 --> 29:21.662
This way, the flowers can truly fulfill their purpose.

428
29:24.862 --> 29:25.622
Sun,

429
29:28.422 --> 29:29.462
I'll...

430
29:30.022 --> 29:31.582
arrange these flowers for you.

431
29:33.102 --> 29:34.062
Fine,

432
29:34.242 --> 29:35.622
but if it's not beautiful, I don't want it.

433
29:36.422 --> 29:37.982
I'll shove it into your hands anyway.

434
29:40.902 --> 29:43.682
First, let's prepare the roses.

435
29:43.702 --> 29:45.602
Alright, everyone, look here.

436
29:45.622 --> 29:48.522
Pluck off any leaves

437
29:48.542 --> 29:50.482
that are below where we'll tie them together.

438
29:50.502 --> 29:52.522
Take them all off to clear it up.

439
29:52.542 --> 29:54.002
Be careful of the thorns, too.

440
29:54.022 --> 29:55.362
Follow my steps.

441
29:55.382 --> 29:57.302
You can cut off the thorns.

442
30:03.062 --> 30:04.502
Hey, need help?

443
30:06.862 --> 30:08.142
Here, I'll help.

444
30:09.782 --> 30:10.862
Be careful of the thorns.

445
30:10.882 --> 30:11.662
You too.

446
30:22.022 --> 30:22.662
Ow!

447
30:33.462 --> 30:34.262
Um...

448
30:34.602 --> 30:36.182
I'll go treat it first.

449
30:55.742 --> 30:57.022
Can I help?

450
31:12.082 --> 31:14.142
Are you very close to Oil?

451
31:15.742 --> 31:17.142
Does it look that way?

452
31:19.802 --> 31:20.582
Yes...

453
31:26.542 --> 31:27.582
We're close.

454
31:28.462 --> 31:29.922
We studied together,

455
31:29.942 --> 31:31.342
worked together,

456
31:32.062 --> 31:34.302
went through good and bad things together.

457
31:36.622 --> 31:37.942
Without her,

458
31:38.042 --> 31:40.142
I wouldn't be here learning about flower arrangement.

459
31:42.382 --> 31:45.542
She seems to be a very important person for you.

460
31:49.342 --> 31:50.682
I admit

461
31:50.702 --> 31:52.022
that she's important to me.

462
31:56.262 --> 31:59.342
Am I intruding on your date with someone important?

463
32:02.942 --> 32:03.942
Are you jealous?

464
32:12.282 --> 32:14.062
How can a friend be jealous of this?

465
32:14.622 --> 32:16.342
I just want to tell you that

466
32:17.662 --> 32:19.382
if we hadn't met,

467
32:22.102 --> 32:24.422
I wouldn't be taking a flower arrangement class here either.

468
32:29.882 --> 32:31.342
Let's go back inside.

469
32:43.122 --> 32:45.042
Well done, everyone.

470
32:45.062 --> 32:46.662
But don't forget

471
32:46.682 --> 32:49.402
to let the flowers you worked hard to arrange today

472
32:49.422 --> 32:51.102
fulfill their purpose.

473
33:05.062 --> 33:05.942
This is for you.

474
33:07.302 --> 33:08.902
I thought you were joking.

475
33:12.382 --> 33:13.862
Well, you know I'm serious.

476
33:18.242 --> 33:20.182
So, I'll go to the clinic after this.

477
33:20.662 --> 33:22.382
Wanna grab something to eat?

478
33:35.182 --> 33:36.382
I'm sorry.

479
33:36.642 --> 33:38.822
Maybe next time. I have to go.

480
33:39.062 --> 33:41.582
Can you take this to the clinic for me?

481
33:41.902 --> 33:43.142
I'll see you later.

482
33:44.142 --> 33:44.822
Mm.

483
34:06.802 --> 34:07.642
Chris!

484
34:07.662 --> 34:08.622
Wait for me!

485
34:13.222 --> 34:14.582
Sun, don't cross the road yet!

486
34:17.582 --> 34:18.702
What is it?!

487
34:30.682 --> 34:33.462
I haven't let my flowers fulfill their purpose yet.

488
34:38.342 --> 34:39.462
Me too.

489
34:40.372 --> 34:42.262
I thought I wouldn't be able to give it to you.

490
34:43.382 --> 34:44.462
You have to.

491
34:44.862 --> 34:45.982
It's your goal, isn't it?

492
34:55.102 --> 34:56.022
So...

493
34:56.202 --> 34:57.822
why are you giving me your flowers?

494
35:00.202 --> 35:02.062
To celebrate our meeting.

495
35:02.622 --> 35:03.502
What about you?

496
35:04.162 --> 35:05.782
To say I'm glad I got to see you again.

497
36:05.982 --> 36:06.802
Wow.

498
36:06.822 --> 36:09.222
I was planning to treat you to our first meal together,

499
36:09.702 --> 36:11.622
but you only wanted Pad Thai. That's it?

500
36:12.782 --> 36:13.662
Well, I like it.

501
36:14.862 --> 36:15.942
You do, too.

502
36:17.262 --> 36:18.582
Mm, that's true.

503
36:19.562 --> 36:20.562
How did you know that?

504
36:23.342 --> 36:24.902
- Your water. - Thank you.

505
36:25.182 --> 36:26.242
What would you like today?

506
36:26.262 --> 36:28.462
Two Pad Thais and one fried mussel pancake, no bean sprouts, please.

507
36:29.002 --> 36:29.542
Alright.

508
36:29.682 --> 36:30.702
Thank you.

509
36:34.582 --> 36:35.302
Hey...

510
36:35.942 --> 36:37.062
I'm sorry.

511
36:37.442 --> 36:40.582
I... ordered for you without asking first.

512
36:44.182 --> 36:45.342
No need to.

513
36:46.102 --> 36:47.582
You ordered correctly.

514
36:48.662 --> 36:49.702
How did you know

515
36:51.142 --> 36:52.662
that I don't like bean sprouts?

516
36:55.342 --> 36:56.342
I didn't.

517
36:57.062 --> 36:59.462
When I had to order the food, I just said it without thinking.

518
37:04.082 --> 37:04.902
Why are you smiling?

519
37:07.022 --> 37:08.022
I'm happy.

520
37:08.582 --> 37:09.582
It's like...

521
37:09.602 --> 37:11.462
god is finally on my side.

522
37:16.102 --> 37:17.442
Thank you.

523
37:17.462 --> 37:18.302
Thank you.

524
37:19.822 --> 37:21.182
Hey, kids!

525
37:21.622 --> 37:23.462
What are you doing? Fighting again, huh?!

526
37:25.202 --> 37:25.742
Oh!

527
37:26.802 --> 37:27.662
Come on!

528
37:27.982 --> 37:29.182
Go home!

529
37:29.862 --> 37:30.702
Hey...

530
37:31.222 --> 37:32.702
are the flowers okay?!

531
37:32.842 --> 37:34.142
It's okay, Chris.

532
37:34.422 --> 37:35.382
It's okay.

533
37:36.542 --> 37:37.902
Will it get bruised?

534
37:38.902 --> 37:40.222
It's still pretty.

535
37:41.582 --> 37:43.942
Even if the flowers aren't in a bouquet,

536
37:44.342 --> 37:45.142
they're still pretty.

537
37:54.322 --> 37:55.022
This is it.

538
37:55.782 --> 37:57.382
This is something new my restaurant needs.

539
38:01.982 --> 38:03.342
Thank you so much, Sun.

540
38:18.402 --> 38:20.462
Where've you been today, Chris?

541
38:24.802 --> 38:26.262
Nice flowers.

542
38:27.282 --> 38:28.582
Who gave them to you?

543
38:31.822 --> 38:33.022
It's mine.

544
38:33.502 --> 38:35.262
I took a flower arranging class.

545
38:37.182 --> 38:38.422
With who?

546
38:39.482 --> 38:40.222
My friend.

547
38:41.382 --> 38:42.822
Since when did you have a friend?

548
38:44.002 --> 38:45.362
We met when I was out running.

549
38:47.982 --> 38:49.982
You haven't told me this before.

550
38:51.102 --> 38:52.582
Introduce me to them.

551
38:52.782 --> 38:54.782
I want to get to know your friend, too.

552
38:57.962 --> 38:58.942
Okay...

553
39:07.022 --> 39:08.342
Where are you taking it?

554
39:11.622 --> 39:13.502
You're the same as always, huh?

555
39:19.602 --> 39:20.742
The same...?

556
39:23.682 --> 39:25.302
You like roses.

557
39:26.822 --> 39:28.062
When you were younger,

558
39:28.622 --> 39:31.822
you loved the rose I gave you so much.

559
39:35.162 --> 39:36.662
You don't remember, do you?

560
39:40.662 --> 39:42.182
But I'm glad

561
39:42.702 --> 39:44.622
that you chose these roses.

562
39:46.422 --> 39:48.542
It means deep down...

563
39:49.582 --> 39:51.462
you haven't forgotten me yet.

564
39:53.862 --> 39:55.702
You haven't forgotten about us.

565
40:08.502 --> 40:10.082
Just a bit longer...

566
40:13.122 --> 40:15.582
I miss the you from back then.

567
40:35.102 --> 40:38.622
I want the Chris I know back.

568
40:48.422 --> 40:49.142
Here.

569
40:50.662 --> 40:52.022
Did you buy these to give to people?

570
40:53.182 --> 40:54.062
No,

571
40:54.202 --> 40:55.462
they're offerings for Buddha.

572
40:56.422 --> 40:58.222
Then no thanks. I don't want to take one meant for Buddha.

573
40:58.862 --> 41:00.622
This one isn't an offering.

574
41:01.382 --> 41:02.982
I want to give it to you.

575
41:24.782 --> 41:25.462
Wait!

576
41:49.302 --> 41:51.862
When are you going to stop flirting with someone who already has a girlfriend?

577
41:53.542 --> 41:54.862
They already broke up.

578
41:55.102 --> 41:57.702
That's what everyone who wants someone who's taken says.

579
41:58.182 --> 41:59.782
If she can't make their relationship public,

580
41:59.982 --> 42:01.022
don't play with her.

581
42:07.342 --> 42:09.262
I didn't start it.

582
42:10.382 --> 42:12.982
You saw how she felt about me, right?

583
42:13.002 --> 42:15.142
It doesn't matter how much she likes you.

584
42:15.822 --> 42:17.662
As long as she hasn't broken up with her girlfriend

585
42:17.682 --> 42:19.102
and told you that you're just a friend,

586
42:20.142 --> 42:21.582
doesn't that mean she doesn't choose you?

587
42:27.782 --> 42:30.802
[Third Person]

588
42:33.151 --> 42:35.851
[Third Person]

589
42:36.771 --> 42:38.971
I want to add edible flowers to our dishes.

590
42:39.071 --> 42:40.531
So that we have something new

591
42:40.591 --> 42:41.791
that's pretty,

592
42:41.811 --> 42:43.371
appetizing,

593
42:43.571 --> 42:44.891
and photogenic.

594
42:45.911 --> 42:47.351
I think it could attract more customers.

595
42:47.371 --> 42:48.411
What do you think?

596
42:49.591 --> 42:50.571
I agree.

597
43:00.771 --> 43:01.811
It's pretty interesting.

598
43:02.571 --> 43:03.831
Thanks, Nadear.

599
43:03.851 --> 43:05.091
Thanks, Nan.

600
43:12.271 --> 43:14.291
Something new? Flowers? Really?

601
43:15.391 --> 43:16.811
No other restaurants do this, yeah?

602
43:20.531 --> 43:21.651
How did you agree?

603
43:22.291 --> 43:24.011
Chris is a shareholder as well.

604
43:24.751 --> 43:25.851
I want Chris to do this.

605
43:26.171 --> 43:27.491
You say it's good, but is it good

606
43:27.551 --> 43:28.891
for our business?

607
43:29.131 --> 43:31.251
Or is it for the relationship between you two?

608
43:32.091 --> 43:33.971
Can you stop asking about my personal life?

609
43:34.611 --> 43:36.091
Be more rational, Nadear.

610
43:36.931 --> 43:38.351
Do you really think

611
43:38.371 --> 43:40.091
these edible flowers

612
43:40.231 --> 43:41.371
won't be a waste of our budget?

613
43:41.651 --> 43:43.251
I insist on letting Chris do it.

614
43:43.771 --> 43:45.091
Even if it's bad,

615
43:45.111 --> 43:46.191
wasteful,

616
43:46.211 --> 43:47.151
not worthwhile,

617
43:47.171 --> 43:48.651
or a loss for us.

618
43:49.771 --> 43:51.131
Is that really okay?

619
43:51.571 --> 43:52.891
What are you thinking?

620
43:53.751 --> 43:54.891
Stop fighting.

621
44:00.571 --> 44:02.651
I'll make this flower dish worthwhile

622
44:03.131 --> 44:04.411
and profitable.

623
44:15.811 --> 44:18.011
I don't think your idea is bad.

624
44:18.231 --> 44:20.771
I just said that to get Nan to let you do it.

625
44:21.251 --> 44:23.171
I didn't want to upset you.

626
44:25.691 --> 44:27.411
When will you understand

627
44:28.231 --> 44:30.611
that I don't want you to protect me like this?

628
44:31.411 --> 44:33.051
I want sincerity.

629
44:34.391 --> 44:37.851
When will you stop treating me like someone about to die?

630
44:38.611 --> 44:39.891
You wouldn't know

631
44:41.811 --> 44:43.691
how much pain I was in

632
44:45.251 --> 44:47.251
when you were dying.

633
44:48.711 --> 44:49.531
Chris!

634
44:49.871 --> 44:50.651
Chris!

635
44:54.411 --> 44:56.071
I don't want to see you in pain

636
44:56.091 --> 44:58.131
or see you sad anymore,

637
44:58.811 --> 45:00.771
because I love you!

638
45:01.611 --> 45:03.011
Am I wrong for that?

639
45:03.831 --> 45:06.251
I'm the one who loves you more.

640
45:10.111 --> 45:12.291
Am I that wrong?

641
45:26.551 --> 45:27.611
I'm sorry...

642
45:39.291 --> 45:41.291
You don't want me to feel sad

643
45:43.451 --> 45:45.371
because my idea was that terrible?

644
47:08.091 --> 47:09.731
Didn't you say you wanted to be my friend?

645
47:10.451 --> 47:12.051
Why are you avoiding me?

646
47:18.931 --> 47:20.531
I can't bring myself to see you.

647
47:21.651 --> 47:22.771
I'm an awful person.

648
47:24.631 --> 47:26.371
There's no place where I fit.

649
47:27.931 --> 47:29.851
If it doesn't fit, then why don't you throw it away?

650
47:33.851 --> 47:35.851
Because it used to be amazing, I guess?

651
47:37.391 --> 47:38.731
That's why I can't discard it...

652
47:39.711 --> 47:40.491
What?

653
47:42.091 --> 47:44.371
Then what about the flowers in the dish?

654
47:47.971 --> 47:50.531
It'd be better if I didn't do anything.

655
47:55.291 --> 47:56.011
Let's go.

656
47:58.351 --> 47:59.211
Where?

657
48:00.951 --> 48:03.371
Somewhere to make you stop thinking you're awful.

658
48:17.631 --> 48:23.511
♫The umbrella we once used to share♫

659
48:23.531 --> 48:28.971
♫Two bodies leaning close beneath the rain♫

660
48:29.691 --> 48:35.811
♫I never felt cold in your warmth♫

661
48:35.851 --> 48:40.091
♫Because you were there every time♫

662
48:40.111 --> 48:41.371
Do I hold the light here?

663
48:41.931 --> 48:42.731
Yes.

664
48:43.371 --> 48:44.771
See? It came out beautifully.

665
48:48.871 --> 48:49.651
But...

666
48:50.711 --> 48:52.711
If we do this, won't it be a loss?

667
48:54.791 --> 48:56.811
You can make it profitable.

668
48:57.531 --> 48:58.491
Trust me.

669
48:59.271 --> 49:00.271
Give it a try,

670
49:01.351 --> 49:02.791
so you'll know

671
49:02.811 --> 49:04.411
you're not as awful as you think.

672
49:06.491 --> 49:12.851
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

673
49:12.871 --> 49:13.651
Whoa,

674
49:14.031 --> 49:16.971
The food cost for this flower dish is thirty percent.

675
49:17.811 --> 49:19.471
Then that means...

676
49:19.491 --> 49:21.491
we have around seventy percent profit.

677
49:21.971 --> 49:25.051
I think it could work after we subtract other expenses.

678
49:25.771 --> 49:30.831
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

679
49:30.851 --> 49:32.731
See? You're not awful.

680
49:34.251 --> 49:35.651
I'm good in theory.

681
49:35.931 --> 49:38.651
What if people don't buy it?

682
49:39.651 --> 49:40.491
Well...

683
49:40.891 --> 49:41.771
it's going to be sad.

684
49:42.531 --> 49:44.771
But isn't it sadder

685
49:45.051 --> 49:48.491
if you didn't do what you love,

686
49:49.571 --> 49:52.011
didn't follow your heart?

687
49:52.671 --> 49:54.611
Would life have any meaning that way?

688
49:58.331 --> 49:59.811
Thank you so much, Sun.

689
50:02.211 --> 50:03.331
Can I hug you?

690
50:19.451 --> 50:20.931
You can drop me off here.

691
50:21.211 --> 50:23.171
I can take you home.

692
50:26.791 --> 50:27.731
It's okay.

693
50:27.751 --> 50:29.291
I'll get there myself.

694
50:29.391 --> 50:31.011
You helped a lot already.

695
50:32.231 --> 50:34.051
It's my pleasure.

696
50:35.131 --> 50:36.731
If your car isn't fixed yet,

697
50:37.251 --> 50:38.491
you can call me.

698
50:38.771 --> 50:40.291
Your chauffeur is on standby.

699
50:40.971 --> 50:42.491
Thank you so much, Sun.

700
50:43.331 --> 50:45.291
I stopped feeling like an awful person because of you.

701
50:46.451 --> 50:47.971
You're a "talented one" now, aren't you?

702
50:48.451 --> 50:49.371
Good job.

703
50:50.371 --> 50:51.851
Thank you, really.

704
51:03.491 --> 51:04.691
Are you kissing as thanks?

705
51:07.111 --> 51:07.931
Mm...

706
51:09.691 --> 51:11.571
Friends don't kiss, do they?

707
52:00.531 --> 52:01.371
I'll go now.

708
52:23.391 --> 52:26.091
We were never friends, Chris...

709
52:48.851 --> 52:50.051
I kissed you,

710
52:50.851 --> 52:52.691
because I don't want to be just friends.

711
52:53.131 --> 52:55.131
Even though I can't recall anything,

712
52:55.691 --> 52:57.591
my heart still flutters

713
52:57.611 --> 53:00.091
every time I see that smile.

714
53:01.291 --> 53:04.811
I won't let anyone come between us.

715
53:05.411 --> 53:07.951
Can you give me three months?

716
53:07.971 --> 53:10.831
Three months to go back to how it used to be.

717
53:10.851 --> 53:13.931
I don't want to keep living like this anymore, Nadear.

718
53:32.171 --> 53:42.051
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

719
53:42.071 --> 53:47.171
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

720
53:47.191 --> 53:51.071
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

721
53:51.351 --> 53:57.231
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

722
53:57.251 --> 54:07.031
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

723
54:07.051 --> 54:12.111
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

724
54:12.131 --> 54:16.391
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

725
54:16.411 --> 54:25.291
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

726
54:25.691 --> 54:34.331
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫
